  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Re-development of carpark to provide a single storey dwelling (1 x 1 bed); access off Whitehall Road; amenity space; hard and soft landscaping; boundary treatment; bin / cycle storage",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed development, by reason of its siting, scale, form, proportions and\r\narchitectural approach, would appear as an incongruous and visually constrained\r\nform of development that would fail to respond appropriately to the prevailing\r\ncharacter, appearance and spatial qualities of the surrounding area. The\r\nproposal would result in the permanent infilling of a frontage parcel which\r\ncontributes to the openness and character of the Roxborough Park Conservation\r\nArea, causing less than substantial harm to its significance. This harm would\r\nnot be outweighed by the public benefits of the proposal. Accordingly, the\r\nproposal would fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the\r\nRoxborough Park Conservation Area and would conflict with Section 72(1) of the\r\nPlanning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Paragraphs 212 and\r\n215 of the National Planning Policy Framework, Policies D2, D3 and HC1 of the\r\nLondon Plan (2021) and Policies GR1, GR10, HO3 and HE1 of the Harrow Local Plan\r\n(2021-2041).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The\r\napplicant has failed to provide sufficient information to adequately assess\r\nflood risk and drainage associated with the proposed development, including\r\ndetails relating to finished floor levels, safe access and egress, flood\r\nresilience and resistance measures, surface water drainage, sustainable\r\ndrainage features and their ongoing maintenance. In the absence of this\r\ninformation, the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the proposal\r\nwould appropriately manage flood risk, provide safe access during flood events\r\nor adequately manage surface water runoff. The proposal therefore conflicts\r\nwith Policy SI12 and SI13 of the London Plan (2021), Policy C4 of the Harrow\r\nLocal Plan (2021-2041) and the flood risk and drainage objectives of the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework.&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
